      "Language": "hun",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Efficacy of transdermal isosorbid-dinitrate spray was investigated in 167 of 254 patients with stable angina pectoris. The transdermal application of isosorbid-dinitrate decreased successfully the number of anginal attacks and the sublingual nitroglycerin or isosorbid-dinitrate consumption. Very few side effects were observed and the patients well-being was good during treatment."},
